note bottom of SourceValues
  Actual source guards must prove that every
  normal return carries the primitive value a
  callback receives. Type assertions and
  manufactured AST nodes cannot provide valid
  evidence from an imported reader.
end note

note bottom of SourceFrames
  A native frame binds callback values to the
  same proven receiver and actual source call.
  Sorting reorders that array, so proving a
  primitive comparator cannot waive effects or
  excuse a changed method.
end note

