note bottom of SourceGate
  A seeded cycle may converge without proving
  that every dependent route is closed and
  grounded. Callback permission requires a
  nonempty universal proof, so unknown routes
  cannot disappear behind one matching target.
end note

note bottom of SourceEpoch
  New mutation facts invalidate every cached
  result before another positive proof can
  consume it. Stable epoch tags prevent stale
  summaries from proving a later scan safe after
  callable or intrinsic facts change.
end note

note bottom of SourceBounds
